## F1 — exact Ray Script expectation rejects the selected native adapter

At **line 954**, `_validation_freeze_error` requires `actor.get_script().resource_path` to equal `res://scripts/acts/act2/ray_scout_actor.gd`. The selected `b81f` London constructor (lines 88–100) creates these actual Ray nodes with `WeybridgeScoutActor`. `weybridge.gd:6` preloads `res://scripts/acts/act2/weybridge_scout_actor.gd`; that adapter extends the base Ray script and does not replace its Script during configuration. Its actual Script therefore has the derived resource path.

The mismatch makes every such mapped pristine recipient ineligible. Lines 882–889 explicitly fail a mapped ineligible recipient even if no cleanup callback occurs. This conclusion follows from selected source; it is not an inferred or reported native failure.

Root may make exactly this one replacement in a **new private test copy**, preserving the owner’s frozen b680 source and all 28 package paths:

```diff
-actor.get_script().resource_path != "res://scripts/acts/act2/ray_scout_actor.gd"
+actor.get_script().resource_path != "res://scripts/acts/act2/weybridge_scout_actor.gd"
```

There is exactly one occurrence of the predicate. Keep the base source-map entry at line 24, the derived entry at line 25, and all same-node/actor-ID/frozen-Script/provenance/lifecycle/HP/profile/lease/private-record/exact-payload checks. This needs no subclass tolerance, production change, new API or signal suppression.

**No new source pin is needed.** SOURCE44 already pins the adapter at line 25 to `7e90bfc541c467162a5a0b0afd6891e8aa6dda9835a4da05362e9301eed78916` (1,129 bytes, actual mode 0600). Its source and UID slot already belong to the previous 201 fixed slots plus four runtime subjects (205 total).

